  "summary": "Black metal trays wreathed in oil-painted garden bouquets — Moscow workshop floral ware.",
  "description": "Zhostovo's iron trays carry the Russian garden in oil: dense rose-and-peony bouquets with poppies, daisies and grape sprays, brushed wet-on-wet over black, red or deep-green enamel grounds, highlighted with fine whites and rimmed with thin gold lace borders. Village workshops from the 1820s (Osip Vishnyakov's among them) turned industrial trays into table jewels; the same five-stroke flower grammar paints panels, brooches and tea caddies. The 1960-established factory keeps masters painting every tray by hand.",
